; Experimental LoTW enrollment challenge, version 1.
; The TQSL signature is a separately policy-gated RSA/SHA-1 assertion. It is
; never an ARAP content proof or COSE signature. Exact challenge bytes are
; signed by both the callsign certificate key and the ARAP Ed25519 key.

enrollment-challenge = {
  1: "ARAP-LoTW-enrollment",
  2: 1,
  3: "bind-ed25519-key",
  4: tstr .size (1..256),       ; exact verifier audience
  5: callsign,
  6: bstr .size 32,             ; SHA-256(DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo)
  7: bstr .size 32,             ; CSPRNG nonce
  8: uint,                      ; issued_at
  9: uint,                      ; expires_at, max 300 seconds after issued_at
}

; The transport response carries exact challenge bytes, a leaf-first DER chain,
; raw Ed25519 public key, raw TQSL data-block signature, and Ed25519 signature.
; Chain size is at most 65536 bytes and at most 8 certificates.
;
; Acceptance additionally requires: current trusted chain; digitalSignature
; key usage when keyUsage is present; issuer-specific callsign extraction;
; configured, timestamped status == good and within verifier max-age; both
; signatures valid; exact key fingerprint;
; audience and time match; and atomic one-time challenge consumption.
callsign = tstr .size (3..20)
